  triage:description "crates/atm-error/src/error_codes.rs:128, crates/atm-storage/src/error_catalog.rs:74 -- D2 requires typed rejections for v1/v2 compatibility failure and states explicitly type-only completion is insufficient. AC10 requires concrete-adapter tests for every public error code. git grep returns exactly the declaration, Display/FromStr mapping, and catalog entry -- zero call sites in any writer/migration/projection code, and zero tests reference it. It is unreachable dead code. Fix: wire TaskCompatibilityFailed into an actual v1/v2 reconciliation failure path (e.g. bridge-trigger reentrancy handling or migration path) and add a concrete-adapter test, or remove it from AC10/D2 scope via explicit sprint-doc amendment if no such path is architecturally reachable this sprint." ;
